(How The Seed Was Built) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The generator creates realistic but synthetic gym usage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Main rules:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- users train `4-6` times per week) Tj
T*
(- each training day uses `4-5` machines) Tj
T*
(- sessions vary by goal, machine, and calibration) Tj
T*
(- reps include valid and invalid attempts) Tj
T*
(- some sessions include fatigue and warning patterns) Tj
T*
(- body metrics and feedback are included separately from device data) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This means the seed is good for UI testing, filtering, and chart validation, but) Tj
T*
(it is still synthetic data, not a physiological model.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Best Ways To Explore It) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(If you want to understand the file quickly, inspect it in this order:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. `usersByRfid`) Tj
T*
(2. `machineConfigs`) Tj
T*
(3. one user under `athleteWeeklySessions`) Tj
T*
(4. one week) Tj
T*
(5. one day) Tj
T*
(6. one session) Tj
T*
(7. that session?s `summary`, `analysis`, `setDetails`, and `repSets`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(That path gives you the whole mental model without needing to read the entire) Tj
T*
(file.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Recommended Dashboard Tests) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
